1. The person in whose favour this licence is issued shall.-
(a)
Comply with all the relevant provisions of the Act and Rules for the time being in force;
(b)
Note encourage or countenance any infringement of the provisions of the Act. or the Rules amended from time to time;
(c)
Exhibit this licence in some conspicuous part of the premises to which it relates;
(d)
Comply with any general or special directions that may be given by the Controller of legal metrology ;
(e)
Surrender the licence in the event of closure of business and / or cancellation of Licence ;
(f)
Present the weights, measures, weighing or measuring instruments as the case any be manufactured and meant for use
within the State, to the legal metrology officer for verification and stamping before sale ;
(g)
Submit the application for renewal of this licence as required under the rules within thirty days of expiry of the validity of
the licence.

